<section class="cs-interventions">
  <div class="cs-interventions-inner">
    <h2 class="cs-h2">How we simplified the account without losing control</h2>

    <div class="cs-intervention-list">
      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Mapped where conversion volume was concentrated</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">Two product groups (core outdoor gear and accessories) accounted for 83% of purchase conversions and an even larger share of revenue. That concentration showed us where separate campaign complexity was, and was not, justified.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Consolidated 14+ campaigns into two focused structures</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">We paused the fragmented legacy structures and reorganized the account around one Performance Max campaign and one Brand Defense campaign. Conversion volume that had previously been distributed across more than 14 campaigns was concentrated into structures with clearer roles and more campaign-level data.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Connected verified customer data through Customer Match</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">Before launching the rebuilt Performance Max structure, we connected verified purchaser history through Customer Match. This gave Performance Max an additional first-party audience signal based on actual customers rather than relying only on platform-observed behavior. The rebuilt campaign showed signs of stabilizing within approximately three weeks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">04</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Aligned ROAS targets more closely with category margins</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">We incorporated the client's category-level margin data into the bidding framework. Higher-margin categories could support more aggressive acquisition at a lower ROAS target while preserving the desired profit outcome. Lower-margin categories required tighter efficiency constraints. The objective was to optimize toward business economics, not one blended efficiency target applied equally to every product.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

